title: Links can point to any part of a document.
pid: 28b3ff10-72e0-44cc-aa45-616702cbf24c
body: |2-
  Links point to nodes (or, equivalently, to branches).

  The target of every link is a node. If the target is a document root, we can say the link points to the entire document. But it might point to some other node deeper in the document.

  For example, consider a document called =eggs= like this:
  #+begin_example
    * eggs
    ** health
    *** protein
    *** cholesterol
    ** recipes
    ** mystical
    *** Which came first, the chicken or the egg?
  #+end_example
  The document branches into three parts: =health=, =recipes= and =mystical=. A link could be to the whole document, or to the =eggs / health= branch, or the =eggs / health / protein= branch. (The last branch mentioned would probably be about the protein in eggs, but the app does not constrain how a user should interpret a path like =eggs / health / protein=.)
contains:
- f0b8d4ce-a66a-4253-8851-1e414335a7a3
